commit a8cb1e5f
author: cdvankammen
date: 2026-10-22 14:04:00 -0600
subject: feat(failover): L1 in-app peer forwarding — settings.peerNodes

- settings: new peerNodes array (default []) for L1 peer forwarding
- custom-server.js: L1 hook — for /v1* requests, when the LOCAL node is
  degraded (health probe failing) AND a healthy peer is configured, forward
  to the peer (streaming-safe, no buffering, x-9r-failover loop protection)
- Local probe uses the ACTUAL listening port (server.address().port), not
  env PORT (which the tray/CLI doesn't set — was a real bug: probe hit :3000)
- Covers 'node up but unusable' (DB lock / provider meltdown / hung) —
  complements the L2 standalone proxy (node-DOWN)
- Tested: 5/5 decision-logic cases (forward/local-first/non-v1/loop/no-peer);
  E2E forward path verified (request reaches peer, response pipes back)


